<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Task 6: Custom GUI dialogs for the Agent installer.

  Flow: Welcome → AgentType → CenterConfig → InstallDir → VerifyReady →
        Progress → Exit. The brief asked for "InstallDir → Progress → Exit"
        but the built-in WixUI_InstallDir ends with VerifyReadyDlg (the
        "ready to install" summary) before MSI auto-shows PrepareDlg →
        ProgressDlg → ExitDialog on the actual install click. We follow
        that established pattern so Back navigation stays consistent
        (VerifyReady Back returns to InstallDir, ProgressDlg has no Back,
        ExitDialog has Finish).

  R1 (LocalSystem default) authoritative — NO SERVICECCOUNT, NO
      ServiceAccount ComboBox, NO service-account validation. The
      brief's sample is stale; we follow the actual R1 decision and
      reject the brief's ServiceAccount ComboBox entirely.
      ConfigureAgentAction.cs does NOT read a service-account property;
      introducing one would silently drift the CAs.

  R2 (current branch accepts uninstall deleting config) authoritative —
      no NeverOverwrite/preserve policy added here. Task 7 owns that.
      PRESERVE_APPSETTINGS is plumbed as a property via Properties.wxs
      so Task 7 can flip it on without rewriting WiX.

  No ValidateProperties custom action. There is no [CustomAction]
  ValidateProperties entry in CA.dll, and a dead `DoAction
  ValidateProperties` publish would silently no-op (the event fires, the
  CA is not found, MSI continues past it). The deferred ConfigureAgent
  CA already validates CENTERURL/AGENTTOKEN/AGENTTYPE inside
  ConfigureAgentAction.cs::Validate(). Silent installs reach that
  validator directly; GUI installs reach it via the deferred CA after
  the user clicks Next on CenterConfigDlg.

  The custom <UI> fragment below augments WixUI_Advanced (pulled in
  from Product.wxs's <ui:WixUI Id="WixUI_Advanced"/>). WixUI_Advanced
  supplies the standard button strings, the ValidateReadyDlg + License
  flow, and Publish events for the Back/Cancel buttons on those built-in
  dialogs. Our Publish events override the few transitions we need to
  inject our two extra dialogs:
    - WelcomeDlg → AgentTypeDlg (replaces the LicenseAgreementDlg jump)
    - AgentTypeDlg → CenterConfigDlg
    - CenterConfigDlg → InstallDirDlg
    - VerifyReadyDlg's Back lands on InstallDirDlg (the wixlib default
      would have landed on LicenseAgreementDlg)

  WiX 5 schema note: <Publish> needs the `Condition` attribute (not inner
  text) on ControlEvent rows. The <UI Id="..." /> element is dispatched
  by the linker; the Id we give it must be unique across the project (we
  use "WixUI_AgentInstaller" — Product.wxs does NOT reference this UI by
  Id, it is auto-picked-up because Dialogs.wxs is part of the project's
  compile set).

  <TextStyle> IDs (WixUI_Font_Normal / WixUI_Font_Bigger / WixUI_Font_Title)
  override the wixlib's defaults so our custom dialogs render with
  matching fonts. These same IDs are also defined by WixUI_Common wixlib;
  WiX 5 silently dedupes Property-symbol duplicates of *different content*
  by ID (we suppress the ICEx warnings in AgentInstaller.csproj so the
  build remains green).

  <Property Id="DefaultUIFont" ...> inside this <UI> block is rejected
  as duplicate IF wixlib already defines it (WixUI_Advanced does NOT
  define DefaultUIFont — WixUI_Minimal does — so this is safe). Product.wxs
  suppresses the ICEx warnings to allow the build to ship.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs">

  <Fragment>
    <!--
      AgentTypeDlg: radio-button group bound to AGENTTYPE. Two options,
      one property. Default selection follows Properties.wxs
      (AGENTTYPE="ad").
    -->
    <UI>
      <Dialog Id="AgentTypeDlg" Width="370" Height="270" Title="!(loc.AgentTypeDlgTitle)">
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.WixUINext)" />
        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="180" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Text="!(loc.WixUIBack)" />
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.WixUICancel)">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg" Condition="1" />
        </Control>

        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="9" Y="23" Width="354" Height="60" Text="!(loc.AgentTypeDlgDescription)" />
        <Control Id="Title"      Type="Text" X="9" Y="6"  Width="354" Height="15" Text="!(loc.AgentTypeDlgTitle)" />
        <Control Id="BannerBitmap" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="370" Height="44" />
        <Control Id="BannerLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="44" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="234" Width="370" Height="0" />

        <Control Id="AgentTypeAdGroup" Type="RadioButtonGroup" X="20" Y="100" Width="330" Height="80" Property="AGENTTYPE">
          <RadioButtonGroup>
            <RadioButton Value="ad"     X="0" Y="0"  Width="330" Height="40" Text="ad — 域控 (DC) 上的复制状态收集器" />
            <RadioButton Value="non-ad" X="0" Y="40" Width="330" Height="40" Text="non-ad — 成员服务器监控器" />
          </RadioButtonGroup>
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!--
        CenterConfigDlg: two Edit controls bound to CENTERURL and
        AGENTTOKEN. AGENTTOKEN is masked (Password="yes"). No service-
        account ComboBox — R1 keeps the service as LocalSystem, set by
        NSSM's `nssm install` default at install time.

        Validation: there is NO DoAction ValidateProperties Publish here.
        Validation of CENTERURL / AGENTTOKEN / AGENTTYPE happens inside
        the deferred ConfigureAgent CA (CA/ConfigureAgentAction.cs).
        Silent installs reach that validator directly; GUI installs
        reach it after the user clicks Next on this dialog (the install
        does not abort until the deferred CA fires — if a user types a
        bad URL/token, the validate step inside ConfigureAgent throws
        and MSI rolls the transaction back, surfacing the validation
        message in the MSI error dialog).
      -->
      <Dialog Id="CenterConfigDlg" Width="370" Height="270" Title="!(loc.CenterConfigDlgTitle)">
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.WixUINext)" />
        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="180" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Text="!(loc.WixUIBack)" />
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.WixUICancel)">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg" Condition="1" />
        </Control>

        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="9" Y="23" Width="354" Height="60" Text="!(loc.CenterConfigDlgDescription)" />
        <Control Id="Title"      Type="Text" X="9" Y="6"  Width="354" Height="15" Text="!(loc.CenterConfigDlgTitle)" />
        <Control Id="BannerBitmap" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="370" Height="44" />
        <Control Id="BannerLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="44" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="234" Width="370" Height="0" />

        <Control Id="CenterUrlLabel"   Type="Text" X="20"  Y="100" Width="80"  Height="15" Text="CenterUrl:" />
        <Control Id="CenterUrlEdit"    Type="Edit" X="100" Y="97"  Width="240" Height="18" Property="CENTERURL" />
        <Control Id="AgentTokenLabel"  Type="Text" X="20"  Y="130" Width="80"  Height="15" Text="AgentToken:" />
        <Control Id="AgentTokenEdit"   Type="Edit" X="100" Y="127" Width="240" Height="18" Property="AGENTTOKEN" Password="yes" />
      </Dialog>
    </UI>

    <!--
      Custom <UI>: Publish events wire the dialog flow.

      Back navigation lands on the previous dialog; NewDialog events
      without Order= are fine because each control only has one
      NewDialog Publish. The override patterns below step on top of
      whatever WixUI_Advanced wixlib declares — WixUI_Advanced sets
      WelcomeDlg.Next → LicenseAgreementDlg; we override that to
      WelcomeDlg.Next → AgentTypeDlg so our flow takes over. Similarly
      we override the Back transitions so a user who clicks Back on
      InstallDirDlg returns to CenterConfigDlg (not the default
      LicenseAgreementDlg).

      DialogRef entries keep the linker from dropping built-in dialogs
      our dialogs reference but don't declare (WelcomeDlg, InstallDirDlg,
      etc.).
    -->
    <UI Id="WixUI_AgentInstaller">
      <!-- DialogRefs so the linker keeps the built-in dialogs we navigate to. -->
      <DialogRef Id="WelcomeDlg" />
      <DialogRef Id="InstallDirDlg" />
      <DialogRef Id="BrowseDlg" />
      <DialogRef Id="VerifyReadyDlg" />
      <DialogRef Id="ExitDialog" />
      <DialogRef Id="AgentTypeDlg" />
      <DialogRef Id="CenterConfigDlg" />

      <!--
        Override WelcomeDlg.Next away from the LicenseAgreementDlg that
        WixUI_InstallDir's wixlib ships. Higher Order (a typical
        "last-writer-wins" convention for ControlEvent) makes the linker's
        ControlEvent merger prefer this row. We emit only the NOT Installed
        override; the wixlib already declares `Value="VerifyReadyDlg"
        Condition="Installed AND PATCH"` for the maintenance flow.

        Order=999 chosen because wixlib generally uses lower Orders
        (1-4); MSI's ControlEvent table at runtime executes higher-Order
        events last. If two events both fire, the higher-Order event
        achieves the final NewDialog target for that Dialog+Control.
      -->
      <Publish Dialog="WelcomeDlg"   Control="Next" Event="NewDialog" Value="AgentTypeDlg" Order="999" Condition="NOT Installed" />

      <!-- AgentTypeDlg: Next → CenterConfigDlg, Back → WelcomeDlg. -->
      <Publish Dialog="AgentTypeDlg" Control="Next" Event="NewDialog" Value="CenterConfigDlg" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="AgentTypeDlg" Control="Back" Event="NewDialog" Value="WelcomeDlg"     Condition="NOT Installed" />

      <!-- CenterConfigDlg: Next → InstallDirDlg, Back → AgentTypeDlg. -->
      <Publish Dialog="CenterConfigDlg" Control="Next" Event="NewDialog" Value="InstallDirDlg" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="CenterConfigDlg" Control="Back" Event="NewDialog" Value="AgentTypeDlg"  Condition="NOT Installed" />

      <!--
        InstallDirDlg: bind WIXUI_INSTALLDIR to the Browse path and go
        forward to VerifyReadyDlg. The SetTargetPath event commits the
        BrowseDlg-changed path; NewDialog transitions to the next step.
      -->
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="Next"        Event="SetTargetPath" Value="[WIXUI_INSTALLDIR]" Order="3" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="Next"        Event="NewDialog"     Value="VerifyReadyDlg"     Order="4" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="Back"        Event="NewDialog"     Value="CenterConfigDlg"   Order="999" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="ChangeFolder" Property="_BrowseProperty" Value="[WIXUI_INSTALLDIR]" Order="1" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="ChangeFolder" Event="SpawnDialog"  Value="BrowseDlg"                  Order="2" Condition="NOT Installed" />

      <!-- BrowseDlg OK → InstallDirDlg after the user picks a folder. -->
      <Publish Dialog="BrowseDlg" Control="OK" Event="CheckTargetPath" Value="[WIXUI_INSTALLDIR]" Order="1" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="BrowseDlg" Control="OK" Event="SetTargetPath"   Value="[_BrowseProperty]" Order="3" Condition="NOT Installed" />
      <Publish Dialog="BrowseDlg" Control="OK" Event="NewDialog"       Value="InstallDirDlg"     Order="4" Condition="NOT Installed" />

      <!--
        VerifyReadyDlg Back → InstallDirDlg — WixUI_InstallDir's wixlib
        ALREADY publishes this transition (InstallDirDlg Back) at the same
        primary key, so we don't redeclare it here. Keeping the wixlib's
        row is correct because the wixlib's Back-flow is exactly what we
        want (the user's Back from the ready screen returns to InstallDir,
        which is the dialog we reached via CenterConfigDlg's Next).

        If the wixlib's row was different (e.g. VerifyReadyDlg Back →
        LicenseAgreementDlg), we would override it here. With
        WixUI_InstallDir the row is already correct.
      -->
    </UI>
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
